Residual correlations imply that there is something driving correlation in the residuals beyond causal paths - not necessarily bidirectionally. Unfortunately, I don’t think you have a model structure where you can estimate true bidirectionally - there are no unique predictors of individuals variables involved in bidirectional paths. So, you’re going to have a hard time here. Given your additional responses, I think the question is WHY you want to have a bidirectional path, and if something like grouping and a multi group analysis would be more apropropriate here.

