I tried both; with former one the model doesn't fit. with the latter one, I used the corpcor package to apply shrinkage parameter (it's L2 regularization method, you can check here <https://www.rdocumentation.org/packages/corpcor/versions/1.6.9/topics/cov.shrink>) with the cov.shrink() function; I don't know if I should apply this shrinkage to the original raw data as a metrix or should I apply it to the covariance matrix? Any one could help? I think the actual covariance matrix (without shrinkage) is non-positive definite because determinant is 3.362909e-42

when I use it with original data matrix, I get below warning messages; I write the code and error messages below:

library(lavaan)
library(corpcor)

data <- matrix(data)
cov.shrink<- cov.shrink(data)

is.positive.definite(cov.shrink)
TRUE

